  "worked_solution": "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3x-\u03d5) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3x)\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\u03d5-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3x)\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\u03d5) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\u03d5\\,\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3x)-R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\u03d5\\,\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n7\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3x)-2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3x)=R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3x-\u03d5),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n7\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3x)-2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3x)=(R\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\u03d5)\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3x)-(R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\u03d5)\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3x).\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\u03d5=7 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\u03d5=2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\u03d5}{R\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\u03d5} & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{7} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}\u2061\u03d5 & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{7} \\\\ \u03d5 & =arctan\\,(\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{7})\u22480.460\\text{\u00a0}\\text{rad},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(R\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\u03d5)^{2}+(R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\u03d5)^{2} & ={7}^{2}+(2\\sqrt{3})^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}\u2061\u03d5+{sin}^{2}\u2061\u03d5) & =49+12 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =61 \\\\ R & =\\sqrt{61}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n7\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3x)-2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3x)\u2248\\sqrt{61}\\,sin\\,(3x-0.460).\n$$",
